{"version":"activity-event.v1","id":"AEV-260829-a75e6329e5074e5ec192f76f","sequence":1,"timestamp":"2026-08-29T22:55:33.866487Z","actor":{"principal":{"availability":"unknown"},"agent":{"availability":"known","value":"codex"},"run":{"availability":"unknown"},"session":{"availability":"known","value":"019f7fb5-2434-7f63-aeed-f889cda2682c"},"operator":{"availability":"unknown"}},"subject":{"element_id":"TASK-260717-rk4mi7","element_type":"task"},"source":{"kind":"local_cli","entrypoint":"cmd.runMutate","request":{"availability":"unknown"}},"correlation_id":"COR-260829-d77ae85f81a52bb262d27bd1","causal_order":1,"operation":"content","changes":[{"field":"title","before":{"kind":"text","text":"TASK-260717-rk4mi7: implement-update-settings-ui-and-background-scheduling"},"after":{"kind":"text","text":"Implement macOS update settings and background scheduling"}},{"field":"description","before":{"kind":"text","text":"User-facing update controls on macOS: automatic-check toggle, check-now action, channel selection (stable/pre-release if enabled), and background update scheduling with clear progress and failure states. Must respect the app's menu-bar UX and not steal focus. AC: settings persist; check-now triggers a feed fetch; background schedule honored; UI states (up-to-date, available, downloading, failed) are covered by presentation-model unit tests. Copy is localizable and routed through the M4 localization path."},"after":{"kind":"text","text":"Add menu-bar-native macOS update controls around the accepted Sparkle lifecycle: persisted automatic-check preference, user-initiated Check for Updates, optional stable or pre-release channel selection, background scheduling, and deterministic presentation states. The production host must not steal focus and tests must use injected updater and scheduler seams without installing an update, publishing a feed, activating the system extension, or enabling VPN."}},{"field":"scope","before":{"kind":"text","text":"(define task scope)"},"after":{"kind":"text","text":"In scope: ReluxProxyMac host-only settings/presentation model; persisted non-secret preferences; Sparkle updater configuration and check-now command; injectable scheduler and updater seams; stable/pre-release channel policy only when metadata enables it; localizable English copy through the repository localization path; deterministic Swift Testing coverage for idle, checking, up-to-date, available, downloading, failed, schedule, relaunch, and disabled-automatic-check behavior; focused macOS build and tests. Out of scope: update installation, signed appcast generation/publication, private EdDSA material, Developer ID/notary ceremony, provider changes, system-extension activation, VPN connection, route/DNS changes, iOS, or physical update replacement validation."}},{"field":"acceptance_criteria","before":{"kind":"text","text":"(define acceptance criteria)"},"after":{"kind":"text","text":"1. The macOS host exposes non-focus-stealing menu-bar update settings for automatic checks, Check for Updates, and channel selection only when the configured feed policy enables pre-release updates. 2. Automatic-check and channel preferences persist across lifecycle reconstruction without storing secrets, and the accepted Sparkle controller receives the effective values through a narrow host-only adapter. 3. Check for Updates invokes the injected updater exactly once and background scheduling is deterministic, cancel-safe, idempotent, and suppressed when automatic checks are disabled. 4. A presentation model maps updater lifecycle events to idle/checking/up-to-date/available/downloading/failed states with localizable English copy and no raw URL, signature, key, path, or error-secret leakage. 5. Swift Testing covers persistence, channel gating, check-now, scheduling/cancellation/relaunch, every presentation state, and failure redaction; focused ReluxProxyMac tests and a host build pass without network installation or VPN/system-extension activation."}}]}
